    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) headlining our offensive attack. His high efficiency score is driven by a massive +14% dynamic platoon advantage and a favorable matchup against Andre Pallante, whose slow delivery provides the perfect runway for a stolen base\u2014a critical factor given our emphasis on speed scarcity. **Junior Caminero** (72.75) and **Yordan Alvarez** (71.46) also offer elite upside; **Junior Caminero** benefits significantly from the soft matchup against Walbert Ure\u00f1a, while **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in core play due to his elite 0.425 xwOBA, proving that even against a mediocre SP_xERA, his raw talent floor remains superior to most of the league.\n\nWe are hunting stolen bases against vulnerable pitchers today, which elevates **Colt Keith** (68.51) and **Trea Turner** (63.25) into must-start territory. **Colt Keith**\u2019s lead-off spot against Erick Fedde is particularly enticing, as Fedde\u2019s 5.44 xERA coupled with his susceptibility to the running game offers the Zebras the best path to maximizing category gains in HR and SB simultaneously. Conversely, **Kazuma Okamoto** (66.27) is a sneaky play in the UTIL slot; while he faces a tougher arm in Trevor Rogers, the +16% park factor provides enough of an offensive boost to comfortably keep him in the lineup over marginal options.\n\nThe bench decision process was tightly contested, with **Chase Meidroth** (53.47) falling just short of displacing **Carson Benge** (53.77). While **Chase Meidroth** offered a strong SP skill bonus, the optimizer favored **Carson Benge** due to the wind-out conditions and the premium of his lead-off role. We also opted to keep **Caleb Durbin** (51.44) on the bench; despite his perfect 100% SB efficiency rating against Slade Cecconi, his projected 9th-order slot dragged his total score below our viability threshold. Owners should monitor all lineups closely, as \"Lineup Pending\" status remains a risk factor for several starters, including **Gary Sanchez** and **Dillon Dingler**, whose values fluctuate heavily based on their final confirmed positions.",
